# Third-party admin theme assets - licensed separately, never committed
/public/assets

# 🔴 The owner's handwritten signature, never committed.
#
# `github.com/morpheusadam/kargah` is public. A signature image in a public
# repository is a signature anybody can lift and paste onto a document the
# owner never saw — and git keeps it in the history even after a later delete,
# so this is not a decision that can be taken back by removing the file.
#
# The invoice reads it from `config('accounting.document.signature_image')`,
# and `InvoiceDocument` treats a missing file as "no image" rather than as an
# error, so a clone without it still renders a valid signature block: the rule,
# the name and the issue date. Nothing breaks; the drawing is simply absent.
#
# To install it on a machine: put the PNG at the path the config names.
/public/img/signature.png


# What the browser audits wrote on the last run. The harnesses are worth keeping;
# a snapshot of one machine's findings is not.
/tools/audit/*.json
/storage/app/audit-copy*.sqlite

# SSH credentials for the panel host. Never in git: the repository is public,
# and a key or password in a public history is compromised the moment it lands
# there, whether or not anybody notices. Deleting the file later does not undo it.
/.data/
